      "EVORAO:biosafetyRestrictions": "This virus was isolated in Cameroon when the trivalent oral polio vaccine was in use. Therefore, it is considered as an OPV2/Sabin 2 potentially infected material and must be handled in compliance with the WHO GUIDANCE FOR NON-POLIOVIRUS FACILITIES TO MINIMIZE RISK OF SAMPLE COLLECTIONS POTENTIALLY INFECTIOUS FOR POLIOVIRUSES available at http://polioeradication.org/polio-today/preparing-for-a-polio-free-world/containment/containment-resources/.",
